	(text "J5 XT30 (as on the MES4-Flasher): pin 1 + flat end, pin 2 - chamfered end.\nF1 15A fast fuse (Nano2 2410, 65 V): protects the XT30 and the board copper; the 8.5 A worst case\nstays under its 75 % derating. Each relay output has its own 3 A PTC, so a load short never blows F1.\nQ1 P-MOSFET reverse-polarity block: correct polarity turns it on (Vgs clamped by D8,\nR6 10k to GND_24V); a reversed lead leaves it off. It replaces the Flasher's SS56 Schottky,\nwhich would dissipate ≈ 3-4 W here. AGM60P90D: -60 V, 13 mΩ, ≈ 1 W at 8.5 A: copper on the drain tab.\nD9 SMBJ30A (600 W): surges and spikes from motors and solenoids on the 24 V bus (CIF §7a).\nC1 100 µF / 63 V electrolytic: bulk, and its ESR damps the cable inductance (hot-plug ringing).\nC2 / C3: HF bypass. LED3 green = 24 V present (after Q1).\n+24V feeds the relay contacts, the INA226 VBUS inputs and the sensor supplies."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 17.78 76.2 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "ec0e5cf1-4a26-5ea0-99c2-9487372191f7")
	)
	(rectangle
		(start 198.12 20.32)
		(end 403.86 106.68)
		(stroke (width 0) (type dash))
		(fill (type none))
		(uuid "78ac9aa2-9d36-5e44-bd93-91fa2a61e51b")
	)
	(text "Power budget and noise strategy"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 200.66 22.86 0)
		(effects (font (size 2 2) (bold yes)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "32c1b5cf-cd0a-59a0-b5eb-23dc2b84ba99")
	)
	(text "24 V current: relays ≤ 4 × 2 A (CIF §7; realistic 3-5 A: lamp ~0.3 A, DRL, 1.5 A solenoid), sensors\n2 × ≤ 100 mA, logic DC/DC ≈ 0.15 A, IMU 9 V ≤ 0.5 A + screen 5 V ≤ 0.95 A + door servo ≤ 3 A (page 9).\nRealistic total ≈ 6-8 A. Every load at its limit at once (≈ 13 A) would exceed F1 15A's 75 % derating\n(11 A) and the XT30's 15 A rating: don't stall the servo while all four relays carry 2 A.\n\nNoise and transients, from the cable inwards:\n1. D9 SMBJ30A clamps surges and inductive spikes on the 24 V bus.\n2. C1 electrolytic damps the cable LC: no ringing above 24 V on hot-plug.\n3. C2 / C3 ceramics: low impedance for HF at the input.\n4. Pi filter C2 + L1 + C4 / C5 feeds only the DC/DC: the logic supply is decoupled\n   from the bus, and the converter's switching noise stays off it.\n5. Isolated DC/DC: the grounds meet only at NT1, so relay load currents never flow in GND.\n6. Pi filter F2 + FB1 + C8 / C9 on the module 5 V, and FB2 again on the ADS1232 AVDD.\n7. Flyback diodes at every relay coil (1N4148W) and every output (SS34).\n8. Sensor supplies: 100 mA PTC + 100 nF / 50 V at each terminal."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 200.66 27.94 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "09d82fdf-7671-580c-b0ef-eedb99c35333")
	)
	(rectangle
		(start 15.24 109.22)
		(end 172.72 185.42)
		(stroke (width 0) (type dash))
		(fill (type none))
		(uuid "c7b9dbf5-783a-5551-9d80-2663ea0d6068")
	)
